    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d644">

                <pb facs="0762" n="702" sameAs="frus:frus1895p1/pg702"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Uhl to Sir Julian Pauncefote</hi>.</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-04-09"><hi rendition="#italic">April 9,
                        1895</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 73.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Excellency</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the
                    receipt of your note of the 1st instant, transmitting a copy of a Canadian order
                    in council, granting free entry into Canada to timber booms imported from the
                    United States.</p>
                <p>The Department is much gratified that a reciprocal arrangement has thus been
                    effected between the United States and Canada in regard to the matter in
                    question.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwin F. Uhl</hi>,<lb/><hi
                            rendition="#italic">Acting Secretary.</hi></signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
